	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/20/3/271.abstract%20N2%20-%20Theories%20concerning%20the%20formation%20of%20bedded%20chert%20traditionally%20have%20emphasized%20either%20depositional%20or%20diagenetic%20processes.%20Major%20and%20rare%20earth%20element%20data%20from%20Franciscan%20assemblage%20(Mesozoic)%20and%20Claremont%20Formation%20(Miocene)%20bedded%20chert%20sequences,%20along%20with%20physical%20observations%20such%20as%20the%20presence%20of%20rare%20and%20highly%20corroded%20radiolarians%20in%20shale%20interbeds,%20are%20most%20consistent%20with%20a%20dominantly%20diagenetic%20origin%20of%20chert-shale%20couplets%20and%20are%20incompatible%20with%20many%20depositional%20theories.%20Chemical%20distributions%20between%20Franciscan%20and%20Claremont%20bedded%20chert=shale%20closely%20match%20chemical%20fractionations%20recorded%20by%20Monterey%20Formation%20and%20Deep%20Sea%20Drilling%20Project-sampled%20cherts%20formed%20by%20diagenetic%20SiO2%20dissolution,%20transport,%20and%20reprecipitation,%20suggesting%20that%20diagenetic%20migration%20of%20SiO2%20from%20proto-shale%20to%20proto-chert%20is%20also%20largely%20responsible%20for%20chert-shale%20couplets.%20Identical%20Ce%20anomalies%20(Ce/Ce*)%20found%20in%20immediately%20adjacent%20chert-shale%20layers%20indicate%20that%20turbidites%20or%20other%20transport%20mechanisms%20are%20not%20responsible%20for%20the%20alternating%20beds.%20Neither%20the%20chemistry%20of%20the%20chert-shale%20couplet%20nor%20the%20overall%20stratigraphy%20of%20the%20sequences%20is%20consistent%20with%20couplet%20formation%20being%20caused%20by%20productivity%20fluctuations.%20Chemical%20mass%20balance%20calculations%20reconstructing%20the%20total%20bulk%20sediment%20composition%20suggest%20that%20modern%20siliceous%20sequences%20do%20not%20contain%20enough%20labile%20biogenic%20SiO2%20to%20form%20entire%20stratigraphies%20of%20bedded%20chert.}}

