	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-file-2 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/43/5/459.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20snowball%20Earth%20hypothesis%20predicts%20globally%20synchronous%20glaciations%20that%20persisted%20on%20a%20multimillion%20year%20time%20scale.%20Geochronological%20tests%20of%20this%20hypothesis%20have%20been%20limited%20by%20a%20dearth%20of%20reliable%20age%20constraints%20bracketing%20these%20events%20on%20multiple%20cratons.%20Here%20we%20present%20four%20new%20Re-Os%20geochronology%20age%20constraints%20on%20Sturtian%20(717%E2%80%93660%20Ma)%20and%20Marinoan%20(635%20Ma%20termination)%20glacial%20deposits%20from%20three%20different%20paleocontinents.%20A%20752.7%20%C2%B1%205.5%20Ma%20age%20from%20the%20base%20of%20the%20Callison%20Lake%20Formation%20in%20Yukon,%20Canada,%20confirms%20nonglacial%20sedimentation%20on%20the%20western%20margin%20of%20Laurentia%20between%20ca.%20753%20and%20717%20Ma.%20Coupled%20with%20a%20new%20727.3%20%C2%B1%204.9%20Ma%20age%20directly%20below%20the%20glacigenic%20deposits%20of%20the%20Grand%20Conglomerate%20on%20the%20Congo%20craton%20(Africa),%20these%20data%20refute%20the%20notion%20of%20a%20global%20ca.%20740%20Ma%20Kaigas%20glaciation.%20A%20659.0%20%C2%B1%204.5%20Ma%20age%20directly%20above%20the%20Maikhan-Uul%20diamictite%20in%20Mongolia%20confirms%20previous%20constraints%20on%20a%20long%20duration%20for%20the%20717%E2%80%93660%20Ma%20Sturtian%20glacial%20epoch%20and%20a%20relatively%20short%20nonglacial%20interlude.%20In%20addition,%20we%20provide%20the%20first%20direct%20radiometric%20age%20constraint%20for%20the%20termination%20of%20the%20Marinoan%20glaciation%20in%20Laurentia%20with%20an%20age%20of%20632.3%20%C2%B1%205.9%20Ma%20from%20the%20basal%20Sheepbed%20Formation%20of%20northwest%20Canada,%20which%20is%20identical,%20within%20uncertainty,%20to%20U-Pb%20zircon%20ages%20from%20China,%20Australia,%20and%20Namibia.%20Together,%20these%20data%20unite%20Re-Os%20and%20U-Pb%20geochronological%20constraints%20and%20provide%20a%20refined%20temporal%20framework%20for%20Cryogenian%20Earth%20history.}}

