	bdsk-url-1 = {http://www.sciencemag.org/content/early/2013/03/20/science.1234204.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20end-Triassic%20extinction%20is%20characterized%20by%20major%20losses%20in%20both%20terrestrial%20and%20marine%20diversity,%20setting%20the%20stage%20for%20dinosaurs%20to%20dominate%20Earth%20for%20the%20next%20136%20million%20years.%20Despite%20the%20approximate%20coincidence%20between%20this%20extinction%20and%20flood%20basalt%20volcanism,%20existing%20geochronologic%20dates%20have%20insufficient%20resolution%20to%20confirm%20eruptive%20rates%20required%20to%20induce%20major%20climate%20perturbations.%20Here,%20we%20present%20new%20zircon%20U-Pb%20geochronologic%20constraints%20on%20the%20age%20and%20duration%20of%20flood%20basalt%20volcanism%20within%20the%20Central%20Atlantic%20Magmatic%20Province.%20This%20chronology%20demonstrates%20synchroneity%20between%20the%20earliest%20volcanism%20and%20extinction,%20tests%20and%20corroborates%20the%20existing%20astrochronologic%20time%20scale,%20and%20shows%20that%20the%20release%20of%20magma%20and%20associated%20atmospheric%20flux%20occurred%20in%20four%20pulses%20over%20~600,000%20years,%20indicating%20expansive%20volcanism%20even%20as%20the%20biologic%20recovery%20was%20under%20way.}}

