	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/32/2/105.abstract%20N2%20-%20Coeval%20mafic%20igneous%20rocks%20emplaced%20rapidly%20over%20%E2%88%BC1.5%20%C3%97%20106%20km2%20in%20western%20and%20central%20Australia%20represent%20the%20erosional%20remnants%20of%20a%20late%20Mesoproterozoic%20large%20igneous%20province,%20named%20here%20the%20Warakurna%20large%20igneous%20province.%20SHRIMP%20U-Pb%20dating%20of%20rocks%20separated%20by%20as%20much%20as%201500%20km%20indicates%20that%20the%20main%20episode%20of%20magmatism%20occurred%20between%201078%20and%20ca.%201070%20Ma.%20The%20Warakurna%20large%20igneous%20province%20includes%20layered%20mafic-%20ultramafic%20intrusions%20and%20mafic%20to%20felsic%20volcanic%20rocks%20and%20dikes%20in%20central%20Australia,%20a%201000-km-long%20mafic%20sill%20province%20in%20Western%20Australia,%20and%20several%20swarms%20of%20mafic%20dikes.%20The%20large%20areal%20extent%20and%20short%20duration%20imply%20emplacement%20above%20a%20mantle-plume%20head.%20Despite%20their%20wide%20separation,%20the%20mafic%20rocks%20have%20similar%20mid-oceanic-ridge%20basalt%E2%80%93normalized%20trace%20element%20patterns%20and%20rare%20earth%20element%20characteristics.%20West-directed%20paleocurrents,%20westward-radiating%20dike%20swarms,%20and%20the%20occurrence%20of%20high-Mg%20rocks%20indicate%20that%20the%20center%20of%20the%20plume%20head%20was%20located%20beneath%20central%20Australia.%20Other%20late%20Mesoproterozoic%20large%20igneous%20provinces,%20in%20the%20Laurentia%20and%20Kalahari%20cratons,%20appear%20to%20be%20significantly%20older%20than%20the%20Warakurna%20large%20igneous%20province%20in%20Australia%20and%20thus%20are%20unlikely%20to%20be%20related%20to%20the%20same%20mantle-plume%20head.}}

