	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://gsabulletin.gsapubs.org/content/89/10/1529.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20Precambrian%20rocks%20of%20the%20Slate%20Islands%20exhibit%20shock%20features%20that%20have%20been%20attributed%20to%20meteorite%20impact.%20The%20islands%20occur%20at%20the%20intersection%20of%20two%20major%20regional%20faults,%20one%20of%20which%20controls%20the%20location%20of%20late%20Precambrian%20alkalic%20magmatism.%20Alkalic%20intrusive%20events%20north%20of%20Lake%20Superior%20occurred%20on%20the%20Slate%20Islands.%20These%20alkalic%20intrusions%20are%20represented%20by%20a%20carbonatite%20dike%20in%20the%20southeast%20corner%20of%20the%20island%20and%20a%20set%20of%20alkalic%20diabase%20dikes%20exposed%20at%20several%20locations%20on%20the%20island.%20Diatreme%20breccias%20cut%20these%20alkalic%20rocks%20and%20are%20interpreted%20to%20be%20late-stage%20phases%20of%20this%20volatile-rich%20alkalic%20magmatism.%20Shatter%20cones%20appear%20spatially%20related%20to%20the%20diatremes,%20and%20quartz%20grains%20displaying%20deformation%20lamellae%20are%20present%20in%20the%20matrix%20of%20the%20breccias.%20Shatter-cone%20structures%20and%20deformation%20lamellae%20are%20considered%20to%20be%20indicative%20of%20shock%20events.%20On%20the%20basis%20of%20field%20observations%20and%20data,%20the%20shock%20and%20diatreme%20events%20can%20be%20correlated%20and%20related%20to%20volcanism%20or%20alkalic%20magmatic%20processes%20associated%20with%20major%20regional%20fractures%20and%20not%20to%20meteorite%20impact.}}

