	bdsk-url-1 = {http://www.sciencemag.org/content/338/6104/238.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20asteroid%20Vesta%20is%20the%20smallest%20known%20planetary%20body%20that%20has%20experienced%20large-scale%20igneous%20differentiation.%20However,%20it%20has%20been%20previously%20uncertain%20whether%20Vesta%20and%20similarly%20sized%20planetesimals%20formed%20advecting%20metallic%20cores%20and%20dynamo%20magnetic%20fields.%20Here%20we%20show%20that%20remanent%20magnetization%20in%20the%20eucrite%20meteorite%20Allan%20Hills%20A81001%20formed%20during%20cooling%20on%20Vesta%203.69%20billion%20years%20ago%20in%20a%20surface%20magnetic%20field%20of%20at%20least%202%20microteslas.%20This%20field%20most%20likely%20originated%20from%20crustal%20remanence%20produced%20by%20an%20earlier%20dynamo,%20suggesting%20that%20Vesta%20formed%20an%20advecting%20liquid%20metallic%20core.%20Furthermore,%20the%20inferred%20present-day%20crustal%20fields%20can%20account%20for%20the%20lack%20of%20solar%20wind%20ion-generated%20space%20weathering%20effects%20on%20Vesta.}}

