	bdsk-url-1 = {http://sp.lyellcollection.org/content/315/1/7.abstract%20N2%20-%20SE%20Asia%20comprises%20a%20collage%20of%20continental%20terranes%20derived%20directly%20or%20indirectly%20from%20the%20India%E2%80%93Australian%20margin%20of%20eastern%20Gondwana.%20The%20Late%20Palaeozoic%20and%20Mesozoic%20evolution%20of%20the%20region%20involved%20the%20rifting%20and%20separation%20of%20three%20elongate%20continental%20slivers%20from%20eastern%20Gondwana%20and%20the%20successive%20opening%20and%20closure%20of%20three%20ocean%20basins,%20the%20Palaeo-Tethys,%20Meso-Tethys%20and%20Ceno-Tethys.%20The%20Sukhothai%20Island%20Arc%20System,%20including%20the%20Linchang,%20Sukhothai%20and%20Chanthaburi%20terranes,%20is%20identified%20between%20the%20Sibumasu%20and%20Indochina%E2%80%93East%20Malaya%20terranes%20in%20SE%20Asia%20and%20was%20formed%20by%20back-arc%20spreading%20in%20the%20Permian.%20The%20Jinghong,%20Nan%E2%80%93Uttaradit%20and%20Sra%20Kaeo%20sutures%20represent%20the%20closed%20back-arc%20basin.%20The%20Palaeo-Tethys%20is%20represented%20to%20the%20west%20by%20the%20Changning%E2%80%93Menglian,%20Chiang%20Mai/Inthanon%20and%20Bentong%E2%80%93Raub%20suture%20zones.%20The%20West%20Sumatra%20and%20West%20Burma%20blocks%20rifted%20and%20separated%20from%20Gondwana,%20along%20with%20Indochina%20and%20East%20Malaya%20in%20the%20Devonian,%20and%20together%20with%20South%20China%20formed%20a%20composite%20terrane%20%E2%80%98Cathaysialand%E2%80%99%20in%20the%20Permian.%20They%20were%20translated%20westwards%20to%20their%20positions%20outboard%20of%20the%20Sibumasu%20Terrane%20by%20strike-slip%20tectonics%20in%20the%20Late%20Permian%E2%80%93Early%20Triassic%20at%20the%20zone%20of%20convergence%20between%20the%20Meso-Tethys%20and%20Palaeo-Pacific%20plates.%20SW%20Borneo%20is%20tentatively%20identified%20as%20possibly%20being%20the%20missing%20%E2%80%98Argoland%E2%80%99%20that%20separated%20from%20NW%20Australia%20in%20the%20Jurassic.%20Palaeogeographical%20reconstructions%20for%20the%20Late%20Palaeozoic%20and%20Mesozoic%20illustrating%20the%20tectonic%20and%20palaeogeographical%20evolution%20of%20SE%20Asia%20are%20presented.}}

