	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://www.sciencemag.org/content/336/6079/335.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20distribution%20of%20seafloor%20ages%20determines%20fundamental%20characteristics%20of%20Earth%20such%20as%20sea%20level,%20ocean%20chemistry,%20tectonic%20forces,%20and%20heat%20loss%20from%20the%20mantle.%20The%20present-day%20distribution%20suggests%20that%20subduction%20affects%20lithosphere%20of%20all%20ages,%20but%20this%20is%20at%20odds%20with%20the%20theory%20of%20thermal%20convection%20that%20predicts%20that%20subduction%20should%20happen%20once%20a%20critical%20age%20has%20been%20reached.%20We%20used%20spherical%20models%20of%20mantle%20convection%20to%20show%20that%20plate-like%20behavior%20and%20continents%20cause%20the%20seafloor%20area-age%20distribution%20to%20be%20representative%20of%20present-day%20Earth.%20The%20distribution%20varies%20in%20time%20with%20the%20creation%20and%20destruction%20of%20new%20plate%20boundaries.%20Our%20simulations%20suggest%20that%20the%20ocean%20floor%20production%20rate%20previously%20reached%20peaks%20that%20were%20twice%20the%20present-day%20value.}}

