	bdsk-url-1 = {http://rsta.royalsocietypublishing.org/content/280/1298/469.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20Precambrian%20apparent%20polar%20wander%20(a.p.w.)%20curve%20for%20Africa%20is%20now%20defined%20in%20a%20general%20way%20from%20ca.%202700%20million%20years%20(Ma)%20to%20Palaeozoic%20times,%20and%20is%20compared%20here%20with%20palaeomagnetic%20results%20from%20other%20Precambrian%20regions.%20Loops%20present%20in%20the%20African%20and%20North%20American%20a.p.w.%20curves%20between%202000%20and%201000%20Ma%20can%20be%20matched%20in%20size%20and%20shape,%20and%20when%20superimposed%20show%20that%20the%20Afro-Arabian%20and%20North%20American%20regions%20were%20in%20continuity%20at%20this%20time.%20Data%20from%20other%20Gondwanaland%20continents%20are%20reviewed%20and%20seem%20to%20be%20consistent%20with%20the%20Smith-Hallam%20reconstruction%20to%20ca.%202100%20Ma%20for%20South%20America,%20to%20ca.%201800%20Ma%20for%20India,%20and%20possibly%20for%20Australia%20back%20to%20ca.%202100%20Ma.%20The%20a.p.w.%20curve%20from%20the%20Baltic%20and%20Ukrainian%20Shields%20can%20be%20matched%20with%20that%20from%20Africa%20and%20North%20America%20such%20that%20there%20was%20crustal%20continuity%20prior%20to%201000%20Ma%20with%20the%20Gothide%20and%20Grenville%20mobile%20belts%20in%20great-circle%20alignment.%20The%20limited%20palaeomagnetic%20data%20from%20the%20Siberian%20Shield%20do%20not%20allow%20it%20to%20be%20placed%20uniquely%20with%20respect%20to%20the%20other%20land%20masses%20but%20are%20consistent%20with%20a%20position%20in%20juxtaposition%20with%20the%20Baltic-Ukrainian%20Shields%20such%20that%20massive%20anorthosites%20and%20ca.%201000%20Ma%20mobile%20belts%20are%20in%20alignment%20with%20those%20from%20elsewhere.%20The%20palaeomagnetic%20evidence%20is%20consistent%20with%20a%20model%20in%20which%20the%20bulk%20of%20the%20Precambrian%20shields%20were%20aggregated%20together%20as%20a%20single%20super-continent%20during%20much%20of%20Proterozoic%20times,%20the%20most%20prominent%20feature%20of%20which%20is%20a%20great%20circle%20alignment%20of%20massive%20anorthosites%20(2250-1000%20Ma)%20along%20a%20belt%20which%20also%20became%20a%20concentrated%20zone%20of%20igneous%20intrusion%20by%20rapakivi%20granites%20and%20alkaline%20intrusions,%20and%20culminated%20in%20generation%20of%20long%20linear%20mobile%20belts%20at%201150%20$%5Cpm%20$%20200%20Ma%20and%20thick%20graben%20sedimentation.%20The%20predominance%20of%20this%20feature%20during%20much%20of%20the%20Proterozoic%20suggests%20that%20a%20simple%20mantle%20convection%20system%20pertained%20during%20this%20time.%20The%20proposed%20super-continent%20is%20not%20greatly%20different%20in%20form%20from%20the%20later%20short-lived%20super-continent%20Pangaea,%20formation%20of%20which%20may%20have%20involved%20relatively%20minor%20redistribution%20of%20the%20sialic%20regions%20in%20late%20Precambrian%20(probably%20post-800%20Ma)%20and%20Palaeozoic%20times.}}

