	year = {2011},
	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-file-2 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://mem.lyellcollection.org/content/36/1/263.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20Tambien%20Group%20of%20northern%20Ethiopia%20(Tigre),%20with%20probable%20correlatives%20in%20Eritrea,%20is%20a%202%E2%80%933-km-thick%20siliciclastic%E2%80%93carbonate%20succession%20that%20was%20deposited%20in%20an%20intra-oceanic%20arc%20platform%20setting%20within%20the%20southern%20Arabian%E2%80%93Nubian%20Shield%20(ANS)%20area%20(southern%20extension%20of%20the%20Nakfa%20Terrane)%20of%20the%20Mozambique%20Ocean.%20Its%20deposition%20occurred%20prior%20to%20ocean%20closure%20between%20converging%20fragments%20of%20East%20and%20West%20Gondwana%20and%20concomitant%20structural%20emergence%20of%20the%20East%20African%20Orogen%20(EAO).%20The%20Tambien%20Group%20is%20well%20exposed%20and%20best%20studied%20in%20the%20Mai%20Kenetal%20and%20Negash%20synclinoria,%20where%20litho-%20and%20chemostratigraphy%20(including%20%CE%B413Ccarb,%2087Sr/86Sr)%20provide%20the%20basis%20for%20a%20composite%20reference%20section.%20Two%20glaciogenic%20intervals%20have%20been%20suggested%20from%20exposures%20within%20the%20Didikama%20and%20Matheos%20Formation%20in%20the%20Negash%20Synclinorium.%20No%20reliable%20palaeomagnetic%20data%20exist%20to%20constrain%20the%20palaeolatitude%20of%20Tambien%20Group%20deposition%20and%20the%20southern%20ANS,%20but%20palaeogeographic%20reconstructions%20and%20evaporite%20pseudomorphs%20in%20lower%20carbonate%20units%20(Didikama%20Formation)%20imply%20low%20to%20intermediate%20latitudes%20(%3C45%C2%B0).%20Integration%20of%20available%20geochronological%20information%20(regional%20magmatism%20and%20detrital%20zircon)%20suggests%20c.%20775%E2%80%93660%20Ma%20as%20a%20plausible%20window%20constraining%20deposition%20of%20the%20prospective%20glacial%20intervals.The%20Tambien%20Group%20appears%20to%20preserve%20a%20coherent%20chemostratigraphic%20framework%20that%20can%20be%20effectively%20subdivided%20according%20to%20shifts%20in%20%CE%B413Ccarb%20polarity%20%5Bpolarity%20intervals%20A%20(+),%20B%20(%E2%80%93),%20C%20(+),%20D%20(%E2%80%93)%5D.%20Slates%20underlying%20and%20interstratified%20with%20polarity%20interval%20A%20carbonate%20preserve%20evidence%20of%20extreme%20chemical%20weathering%20that%20lessened%20prior%20to%20deposition%20of%20polarity%20interval%20B%20carbonate.%20Tambien%20Group%20carbonate%20units%20have%20sedimentological%20characteristics%20consistent%20with%20both%20shallow%20and%20deeper%20marine%20depositional%20settings.%20The%20lower%20prospective%20glacial%20interval%20lacks%20diagnostic%20sedimentological%20evidence%20of%20synglacial%20deposition,%20but%20is%20overlain%20by%20negative%20%CE%B413C%20carbonate%20(polarity%20interval%20B)%20with%20sedimentological%20characteristics%20consistent%20with%20well-documented%20cap-carbonate%20successions.%20The%20upper%20prospective%20glacial%20interval%20in%20the%20Negash%20Synclinorium%20(Matheos%20Diamictite)%20best%20exhibits%20characteristics%20consistent%20with%20glaciogenic%20deposition%20(matrix-supported%20polymictic%20clasts,%20possible%20dropstones,%20possible%20bullet-nosed%20and%20striated%20clasts).%20In%20contrast%20to%20pericratonic%20rift%20margin%20settings%20that%20are%20common%20for%20Cryogenian%20glaciogenic%20deposits,%20palaeogeographic%20reconstructions%20for%20the%20775%E2%80%93660%20Ma%20timeframe%20place%20northern%20Ethiopia%20within%20an%20intra-oceanic%20setting%20that%20was%20likely%20far%20removed%20from%20cratonic%20hinterlands.%20More%20work%20on%20Tambien%20Group%20sedimentology,%20geochronology%20and%20palaeogeography%20is%20required%20to%20better%20evaluate%20the%20extent%20and%20timing%20of%20glacial%20conditions%20associated%20with%20the%20prospective%20glaciogenic%20intervals.Supplementary%20material:%20Supplementary%20Table%2021.1%20of%20Tambien%20Group%20geochronological%20age%20constraints%20is%20available%20at%20http://www.geolsoc.org.uk/SUP18462.}}

