	title = {{The North Shore Volcanic Group: Mesoproterozoic plateau volcanic rocks of the Midcontinent Rift System in northeastern Minnesota}},
	ty = {JOUR},
	volume = {24},
	year = {2011},
	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://fieldguides.gsapubs.org/content/24/121.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%207%E2%80%939-km-thick%20North%20Shore%20Volcanic%20Group%20(NSVG)%20constitutes%20the%20volcanic%20products%20of%20the%201.1%20Ga%20Midcontinent%20Rift%20System%20in%20northeastern%20Minnesota.%20With%20close%20physical,%20chemical,%20and%20volcanological%20analogies%20to%20Tertiary-to-modern%20Iceland,%20these%20flows%20accumulated%20in%20a%20gradually%20subsiding%20basin%20over%20a%20mantle%20plume%20centered%20beneath%20modern%20Lake%20Superior%20between%201108%20and%201094%20Ma.%20They%20are%20essentially%20undeformed,%20except%20for%20local%20faulting%20and%20disruption%20associated%20with%20hypabyssal%20intrusions.Geochemically%20the%20NSVG%20is%20bimodal,%20dominated%20by%20basalts%20and%20rhyolites,%20but%20includes%20a%20complete%20tholeiitic%20Fe-enrichment%20suite%20that%20ranges%20from%20primitive%20olivine%20tholeiite%20through%20transitional%20basalt,%20basaltic%20andesite,%20andesite,%20and%20icelandite%20to%20rhyolite.%20The%20mafic%20magmas%20were%20partial%20melts%20of%20the%20plume%20and%20lithospheric%20mantle,%20variably%20modified%20by%20crystal%20fractionation%20in%20crustal%20chambers%20and%20by%20crustal%20interaction.%20Many,%20but%20not%20all,%20of%20the%20rhyolites%20were%20derived%20largely%20from%20partial%20melting%20of%20Archean%20crust.The%20volcanic%20rocks%20were%20erupted%20subaerially,%20primarily%20from%20fissures,%20though%20there%20is%20some%20evidence%20for%20central%20volcanoes.%20Some%20of%20the%20rhyolites%20are%20very%20large%20and%20widespread,%20and%20were%20emplaced%20as%20high-temperature%20lavas%20and%20rheoignimbrites%20that%20crystallized%20primary%20tridymite.During%20their%20accumulation%20and%20subsidence,%20these%20plateau%20volcanics%20were%20subjected%20to%20burial/hydrothermal%20metamorphism,%20resulting%20in%20secondary%20mineral%20associations%20that%20range%20from%20greenschist%20(epidote-chlorite-albite%C2%B1actinolite)%20to%20zeolite%20(thomsonite-scolecite-smectite)%20facies.This%20field%20trip%20will%20allow%20participants%20to%20examine%20outcrops%20throughout%20the%20stratigraphic%20section%20of%20the%20NSVG,%20including%20structural%20relations,%20volcanology,%20geochemical%20diversity,%20burial%20metamorphism,%20and%20associated%20hypabyssal%20intrusions.}}

