	bdsk-url-1 = {http://specialpapers.gsapubs.org/content/396/67.abstract%20N2%20-%20Lava%20emplacement%20induces%20numerous%20processes,%20among%20which%20are%20crystallization%20and%20oxidation.%20While%20crystallization%20is%20mainly%20thermally%20driven,%20oxidation%20may%20be%20primary,%20or%20secondary%20if%20an%20environmental%20interaction%20is%20involved.%20Here,%20three%20major%20processes%20are%20considered,%20crystallization,%20volume%20oxidation,%20and%20a%20surface%20alteration%20that%20may%20result%20in%20surface%20oxidation,%20which%20has%20heretofore%20not%20been%20described.%20All%20these%20processes%20are%20shown%20to%20be%20high-temperature%20phenomena%20and%20they%20are%20not%20related%20to%20weathering.%20The%20nature%20of%20these%20processes%20and%20their%20quantification%20is%20elucidated%20by%20isothermal%20heat%20treatment%20experiments%20of%20quenched%20lava%20samples.%20This%20quantification%20allows%20scientists%20to%20delineate%20the%20thermal%20history%20of%20basaltic%20melts%20in%20relation%20to%20their%20textures;%20oxidation%20is%20suggested%20to%20be%20a%20consequence%20of%20crystallization;%20surface%20alteration%20involves%20cation%20migration%20to%20lava%20surfaces%20in%20the%20presence%20of%20an%20oxygen%20gradient,%20resulting%20in%20surface%20oxidation%20if%20the%20migrating%20cation%20is%20iron.}}

