	bdsk-url-1 = {http://mem.lyellcollection.org/content/36/1/93.abstract%20N2%20-%20New%20stratigraphic,%20geochronological%20and%20palaeomagnetic%20constraints%20allow%20updates%20to%20be%20made%20to%20a%20synthesis%20of%20Neoproterozoic%20glacial%20palaeolatitudes,%20including%20modifications%20to%20some%20reliability%20estimates.%20The%20overall%20pattern%20of%20a%20Neoproterozoic%20climatic%20paradox%20persists:%20there%20is%20an%20abundance%20of%20tropical%20palaeolatitudes%20and%20near%20to%20complete%20absence%20of%20glaciogenic%20deposits%20demonstrably%20laid%20down%20between%20latitudes%20of%2060%C2%B0%20and%2090%C2%B0.%20In%20addition%20to%2012%20units%20with%20palaeolatitude%20estimates%20that%20are%20somewhat%20reliable,%20estimates%20with%20moderate%20to%20high%20reliability%20now%20include%20Konnarock%20(less%20than%2010%C2%B0%20from%20the%20palaeo-equator),%20Elatina,%20Rapitan,%20Mechum%20River,%20Grand%20Conglomerat%20(10%E2%80%9320%C2%B0),%20Upper%20Tindir,%20Puga%20(20%E2%80%9330%C2%B0),%20Nantuo,%20Gaskiers%20(30%E2%80%9340%C2%B0)%20and%20Walsh%20(40%E2%80%9350%C2%B0).%20Among%20these,%20Elatina,%20Upper%20Tindir%20and%20Nantuo%20are%20considered%20to%20have%20the%20highest%20reliability,%20all%20with%20estimates%20of%20low%20to%20moderate%20palaeolatitude.%20The%20Elatina%20result%20stems%20from%20sedimentary%20rocks%20with%20quantitative%20correction%20of%20inclination-shallowing%20effects,%20and%20the%20Upper%20Tindir%20result%20stems%20from%20data%20collected%20from%20igneous%20rocks%20that%20are%20precisely%20coeval%20with%20the%20glacial%20deposits.%20Despite%20continuing%20debate%20on%20the%20global%20character%20of%20Neoproterozoic%20ice%20ages,%20their%20pan-glacial%20extent%20(ice%20extending%20to%20low%20latitude%20in%20a%20low-obliquity%20world)%20is%20well%20demonstrated.}}

