	bdsk-file-2 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://www.sciencemag.org/content/early/2011/11/16/science.1213454.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20end-Permian%20mass%20extinction%20was%20the%20most%20severe%20biodiversity%20crisis%20in%20earth%20history.%20To%20better%20constrain%20the%20timing,%20and%20ultimately%20the%20causes%20of%20this%20event,%20we%20collected%20a%20suite%20of%20geochronologic,%20isotopic,%20and%20biostratigraphic%20data%20on%20several%20well-preserved%20sedimentary%20sections%20in%20South%20China.%20High-precision%20U-Pb%20dating%20reveals%20that%20the%20extinction%20peak%20occurred%20just%20before%20252.28%20%C2%B1%200.08%20Ma,%20following%20a%20decline%20of%202%E2%80%B0%20in%20%CE%B413C%20over%2090,000%20years,%20and%20coincided%20with%20a%20%CE%B413C%20excursion%20of%20-5%E2%80%B0%20that%20is%20estimated%20to%20have%20lasted%20%E2%89%A420,000%20years.%20The%20extinction%20interval%20was%20less%20than%20200,000%20years,%20and%20synchronous%20in%20marine%20and%20terrestrial%20realms;%20associated%20charcoal-rich%20and%20soot-bearing%20layers%20indicate%20widespread%20wildfires%20on%20land.%20A%20massive%20release%20of%20thermogenic%20carbon%20dioxide%20and/or%20methane%20may%20have%20caused%20the%20catastrophic%20extinction.}}

