	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://www.sciencemag.org/content/334/6059/1091.abstract%20N2%20-%20Diverse%20bilaterian%20clades%20emerged%20apparently%20within%20a%20few%20million%20years%20during%20the%20early%20Cambrian,%20and%20various%20environmental,%20developmental,%20and%20ecological%20causes%20have%20been%20proposed%20to%20explain%20this%20abrupt%20appearance.%20A%20compilation%20of%20the%20patterns%20of%20fossil%20and%20molecular%20diversification,%20comparative%20developmental%20data,%20and%20information%20on%20ecological%20feeding%20strategies%20indicate%20that%20the%20major%20animal%20clades%20diverged%20many%20tens%20of%20millions%20of%20years%20before%20their%20first%20appearance%20in%20the%20fossil%20record,%20demonstrating%20a%20macroevolutionary%20lag%20between%20the%20establishment%20of%20their%20developmental%20toolkits%20during%20the%20Cryogenian%20%5B(850%20to%20635%20million%20years%20ago%20(Ma)%5D,%20and%20the%20later%20ecological%20success%20of%20metazoans%20during%20the%20Ediacaran%20(635%20to%20541%20Ma)%20and%20Cambrian%20(541%20to%20488%20Ma)%20periods.%20We%20argue%20that%20this%20diversification%20involved%20new%20forms%20of%20developmental%20regulation,%20as%20well%20as%20innovations%20in%20networks%20of%20ecological%20interaction%20within%20the%20context%20of%20permissive%20environmental%20circumstances.}}

