	bdsk-url-1 = {http://www.sciencemag.org/content/334/6059/1121.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20Phanerozoic%20fossil%20record%20of%20marine%20animal%20diversity%20covaries%20with%20the%20amount%20of%20marine%20sedimentary%20rock.%20The%20extent%20to%20which%20this%20covariation%20reflects%20a%20geologically%20controlled%20sampling%20bias%20remains%20unknown.%20We%20show%20that%20Phanerozoic%20records%20of%20seawater%20chemistry%20and%20continental%20flooding%20contain%20information%20on%20the%20diversity%20of%20marine%20animals%20that%20is%20independent%20of%20sedimentary%20rock%20quantity%20and%20sampling.%20Interrelationships%20among%20variables%20suggest%20long-term%20interactions%20among%20continental%20flooding,%20sulfur%20and%20carbon%20cycling,%20and%20macroevolution.%20Thus,%20mutual%20responses%20to%20interacting%20Earth%20systems,%20not%20sampling%20biases,%20explain%20much%20of%20the%20observed%20covariation%20between%20Phanerozoic%20patterns%20of%20sedimentation%20and%20fossil%20biodiversity.%20Linkages%20between%20biodiversity%20and%20environmental%20records%20likely%20reflect%20complex%20biotic%20responses%20to%20changing%20ocean%20redox%20conditions%20and%20long-term%20sea-level%20fluctuations%20driven%20by%20plate%20tectonics.}}

