	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/39/4/319.abstract%20N2%20-%20Neoproterozoic%20deglacial%20stratigraphy%20is%20commonly%20characterized%20by%20a%20sharp%20contact%20separating%20glacial%20sediments%20from%20laminated%20capping%20carbonates.%20This%20stratigraphic%20relation%20is%20generally%20assumed%20to%20have%20time%20significance%20and%20to%20reflect%20an%20abrupt%20shift%20from%20icehouse%20to%20greenhouse%20conditions.%20In%20contrast%20to%20this,%20sequence%20stratigraphic%20field%20studies%20of%20an%20Ediacaran%20(ca.%20635%20Ma)%20glacial%20to%20postglacial%20transition%20in%20the%20Amadeus%20Basin%20of%20central%20Australia%20reveal%20a%20complex%20deglacial%20stratigraphy,%20in%20which%20more%20than%20175%20m%20of%20conglomerate,%20sandstone,%20marl,%20and%20carbonate%20at%20the%20basin%20margin,%20and%20portions%20of%20four%20unconformity-bounded%20sequences,%20pass%20basinward%20into%20no%20more%20than%203%20m%20of%20laminated%20dolomicrite%20of%20typical%20cap%20carbonate%20facies.%20The%20unconformities,%20which%20are%20characterized%20by%20as%20much%20as%20several%20tens%20of%20meters%20of%20erosional%20relief%20(oblique%20sections%20of%20incised%20valleys),%20separate%20intervals%20of%20contrasting%20sediment%20provenance,%20and%20are%20confidently%20mapped%20on%20the%20basis%20of%20both%20criteria.%20Comparable%20unconformities%20are%20absent%20in%20the%20overlying%20Neoproterozoic%20succession,%20which%20is%20%3E2%20km%20thick%20and%20encompasses%20many%20tens%20of%20millions%20of%20years.%20The%20Amadeus%20Basin%20cap%20carbonate%20was%20thus%20deposited%20during%20a%20protracted%20interval%20of%20multiphase%20(cyclical)%20transgression%20more%20similar%20to%20Phanerozoic%20cyclical%20sea-level%20rise%20than%20to%20the%20single%20catastrophic%20deglaciation%20and%20instantaneous%20precipitation%20invoked%20by%20popular%20current%20models%20to%20explain%20the%20classic%20cap%20carbonate.%20The%20superposition%20of%20carbonate%20on%20glacial%20facies%20in%20distal%20sections%20evidently%20records%20condensation%20in%20the%20absence%20of%20siliciclastic%20sediment%20rather%20than%20abrupt%20shifts%20between%20glacial%20and%20tropical%20conditions.%20Facies%20lithologically%20similar%20to%20cap%20carbonates%20may%20be%20less%20obvious%20in%20Phanerozoic%20successions%20because%20of%20a%20secular%20change%20in%20carbonate%20composition%20to%20reefal%20and%20deep-sea%20pelagic%20deposits.}}

