	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/23/2/149.abstract%20N2%20-%20Comparison%20of%20a%20new%20%E2%88%BC1700%E2%80%931600%20Ma%20segment%20of%20the%20Proterozoic%20apparent%20polar%20wander%20path%20(APWP)%20for%20Australia%20with%20the%20time-equivalent%20segment%20of%20the%20North%20American%20APWP%20that%20has%20been%20rotated%20clockwise%20by%20117%C2%B0%20about%20the%20Euler%20pole,%20long%20100%C2%B0E,%20lat%2038%C2%B0N,%20superposes%20the%20North%20American%20APWP%20onto%20the%20Australian%20APWP%20and%20shows%20the%20segments%20to%20be%20similar.%20The%20same%20rotation%20makes%20the%20Pacific%20margins%20of%20the%20North%20American%20and%20Australian%20cratons%20adjacent,%20as%20predicted%20by%20the%20Southwest%20U.S.%E2%80%93East%20Antarctic%20(SWEAT)%20hypothesis,%20but%20North%20America%20is%20located%20farther%20north%20relative%20to%20Australia%20than%20originally%20suggested.%20However,%20the%20reconstruction%20is%20consistent%20with%20the%20identification%20of%20western%20sediment%20sources%20for%20the%20Belt-Purcell%20basin%20in%20western%20North%20America,%20with%20matching%20of%20basement%20provinces,%20and%20with%20correlation%20of%20major%20lineaments%20of%20the%20two%20continents.%20The%20rotation%20gives%20only%20very%20broad%20agreement%20between%20the%20younger%20Proterozoic%20pole%20sets.%20This%20is%20probably%20partly%20due%20to%20the%20sparseness%20of%20poles%20on%20the%20Australian%20APWP%20whereby%20prominent%20features%20that%20are%20found%20on%20the%20North%20American%20APWP,%20such%20as%20the%20Grenville%20loop,%20are%20eliminated%20on%20the%20Australian%20path%20by%20smoothing.%20Nevertheless,%20some%20discrepancies%20between%20the%20younger%20Proterozoic%20poles%20cannot%20be%20accounted%20for%20without%20revision%20of%20the%20APWPs.}}

