	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/early/2011/03/29/G31654.1.abstract%20N2%20-%20Idealized%20conceptual%20models%20of%20supercontinent%20cyclicity%20must%20be%20tested%20against%20the%20geologic%20record%20using%20pre-Pangean%20reconstructions.%20We%20integrate%20tectonostratigraphic%20records%20and%20paleomagnetic%20data%20from%20Siberia,%20Laurentia,%20and%20Baltica%20to%20produce%20a%20quantitative%20reconstruction%20of%20the%20core%20of%20the%20Nuna%20supercontinent%20at%201.9%E2%80%931.3%20Ga.%20In%20our%20model,%20the%20present%20southern%20and%20eastern%20margins%20of%20Siberia%20juxtapose%20directly%20adjacent%20to,%20respectively,%20the%20arctic%20margin%20of%20Laurentia%20and%20the%20Uralian%20margin%20of%20Baltica.%20Consistent%20tectonostratigraphic%20records%20of%20the%20three%20cratons%20collectively%20indicate%20the%20history%20of%20Nuna's%20assembly%20and%20breakup.%20According%20to%20this%20reconstruction,%20the%20late%20Mesoproterozoic%20transition%20from%20Nuna%20to%20Rodinia%20appears%20to%20have%20been%20much%20less%20dramatic%20than%20the%20subsequent%20late%20Neoproterozoic%20transition%20from%20Rodinia%20to%20Gondwana.}}

