	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/33/10/769.abstract%20N2%20-%20A%20U-Pb%20zircon%20sensitive%20high-resolution%20ion%20microprobe%20age%20of%201119.4%20%C2%B1%208.5%20Ma,%20obtained%20from%20a%20quartz%20syenite%20dredged%20from%20the%20South%20Tasman%20Rise%20(Australia),%20provides%20the%20first%20direct%20evidence%20of%20the%20presence%20of%20Grenville-age%20magmatic%20rocks%20along%20the%20central%20part%20of%20the%20hypothesized%20Australia%E2%80%93East%20Antarctica%20conjugate%20margin%20of%20Laurentia.%20The%20distinctive%20mineralogy%20and%20geochemistry%20of%20the%20rock%20and%20its%20Sm-Nd%20and%20Pb%20isotopic%20signatures%201)%20indicate%20that%20it%20represents%20a%20juvenile%20Grenville-age%20addition%20to%20the%20crust,%202)%20support%20a%20correlation%20with%20the%20Grenville%20magmatic%20province%20of%20the%20western%20United%20States,%20and%203)%20set%20a%20unique%20pivotal%20point%20for%20a%20precise%20reconstruction%20of%20Rodinia.%20The%20resulting%20scenario%20implies%20the%20presence%20of%20a%20new%20magmatic%20province%20crossing%20the%20East%20Antarctic%20craton,%20the%20extension%20of%20Proterozoic%20belts%20of%20southwest%20Laurentia%20to%20East%20Antarctica,%20and%20appears%20consistent%20with%20the%20Australia%E2%80%93western%20United%20States%20(AUSWUS)%20model.%20This%20tectonic%20setting%20envisages%20a%20near-local%20source%20for%20the%20ubiquitous%20Grenville-age%20detrital%20zircon%20population%20in%20marginal%20Neoproterozoic%20to%20early%20Paleozoic%20Gondwanan%20sequences%20and%20suggests%20a%20possible%20direct%20source%20for%20the%20widespread%20Grenville-age%20inherited%20zircon%20component%20observed%20in%20most%20Paleozoic%20granites%20in%20northern%20Victoria%20Land%20(Antarctica)%20and%20east%20Tasmania%20(Australia).}}

