	bdsk-file-1 = {},
	bdsk-url-1 = {http://jgs.lyellcollection.org/content/167/1/61.abstract%20N2%20-%20Cratonic%20basins%20form%20within%20stable%20regions%20of%20the%20continental%20interior%20and%20initiate%20during%20periods%20of%20break-up%20and%20dispersal%20of%20supercontinental%20assemblies,%20when%20the%20continental%20lithosphere%20may%20experience%20tensional%20stress.%20We%20investigate%20the%20subsidence%20of%20cratonic%20basins%20using%20a%201D%20forward%20model%20of%20protracted%20stretching%20at%20low%20strain%20rates%20of%20thick%20continental%20lithosphere.%20At%20low%20strain%20rates,%20subsidence%20history%20departs%20from%20the%20uniform%20instantaneous%20model,%20as%20supported%20by%20calculations%20of%20the%20thermal%20P%C3%A9clet%20number.%20Cooling%20as%20a%20result%20of%20upward%20advection%20is%20matched%20by%20thermal%20diffusion,%20producing%20a%20subsidence%20trajectory%20with%20a%20near-constant%20slope%20and%20a%20slight%20elbow%20when%20stretching%20ceases.%20The%20model%20is%20used%20to%20evaluate%20the%20subsidence%20history%20of%20boreholes%20in%20cratonic%20basin-fills.%20Marked%20accelerations%20and%20decelerations%20of%20subsidence,%20attributed%20to%20secondary%20mechanisms%20such%20as%20the%20dynamic%20response%20to%20mantle%20convection,%20are%20removed%20from%20the%20backstripped,%20water-loaded%20subsidence%20curves%20to%20obtain%20the%20%E2%80%98reduced'%20subsidence.%20Fits%20to%20the%20reduced%20curves%20indicate%20strain%20rates%20of%20c.%2010%E2%88%9216%20s%E2%88%921,%20stretching%20durations%20of%2050%20Ma,%20and%20stretch%20factors%20of%20as%20little%20as%201.1%E2%80%931.3,%20despite%20the%20extreme%20longevity%20of%20subsidence.%20Cratonic%20basins%20are%20therefore%20part%20of%20the%20rift%E2%80%93drift%20suite,%20occupying%20a%20portion%20of%20the%20existence%20field%20at%20low%20stretch%20factors%20and%20low%20extensional%20strain%20rate.}}

