	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/39/1/51.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20Paleocene-Eocene%20Thermal%20Maximum%20(PETM;%20ca.%2055.8%20Ma)%20is%20associated%20with%20a%20rapid%20and%20large%20carbon%20cycle%20perturbation,%20transient%20warming,%20and%20deep-sea%20acidification.%20Although%20this%20event%20is%20widely%20known%20from%20pelagic,%20hemipelagic,%20and%20continental%20records,%20the%20lack%20of%20in%20situ,%20shallow-water%20carbonate%20platform%20sections%20inhibits%20interpretations%20of%20whether%20the%20PETM%20had%20a%20significant%20effect%20on%20shallow-water%20carbonate%20ecosystems.%20Limalok%20Guyot%20(Ocean%20Drilling%20Program%20Site%20871)%20in%20the%20Pacific%20Ocean%20comprises%20a%20volcanic%20pedestal%20topped%20by%20a%20Paleogene%20carbonate%20platform%20that%20drowned%20in%20the%20Middle%20Eocene.%20Carbon%20isotope%20stratigraphy%20of%20the%20platform%20carbonate%20sediments%20is%20used,%20in%20conjunction%20with%20existing%20biostratigraphy,%20to%20refine%20the%20stratigraphic%20framework%20of%20the%20carbonate%20platform.%20Although%20core%20recovery%20was%20poor,%20the%20major%20Late%20Paleocene%E2%80%93Middle%20Eocene%20stratigraphic%20trends%20in%20carbon%20isotopes%20are%20recognized,%20including%20a%20prominent%20%E2%88%BC3%E2%80%B0%20negative%20carbon%20isotope%20excursion,%20recording%20the%20onset%20of%20the%20PETM.%20The%20lithological%20and%20paleontological%20record%20of%20the%20PETM%20on%20Limalok%20Guyot%20shows%20no%20major%20evidence%20for%20a%20carbonate%20production%20crisis,%20suggesting%20that%20the%20effects%20of%20any%20changes%20in%20temperatures%20or%20surface%20ocean%20pH%20were%20relatively%20short%20lived%20or%20relatively%20minor.}}

