	bdsk-url-1 = {http://geology.gsapubs.org/content/32/5/437.abstract%20N2%20-%20The%20most%20complete%20Neoproterozoic%20successions%20in%20south%20China%20contain%20three%20diamictite%20intervals%20in%20the%20Changan,%20Tiesiao,%20and%20Nantuo%20Formations.%20The%20youngest%20and%20most%20widespread%20Nantuo%20glacial%20deposit%20overlies%20the%20Datangpo%20Formation%20and%20underlies%20the%20fossil-%20rich%20Doushantuo%20Formation.%20Previous%20authors%20have%20correlated%20the%20Nantuo%20diamictite%20to%20either%20Sturtian%20or%20Marinoan%20glacial%20deposits%20elsewhere.%20Here%20we%20report%20sedimentary%20and%20%CE%B413C%20chemostratigraphic%20data%20of%20the%20Doushantuo%20cap%20dolostone,%20which%20overlies%20the%20Nantuo%20Formation.%20Facies-dependent%20variation%20in%20%CE%B413C%20is%20interpreted%20as%20evidence%20for%20spatial%20heterogeneity%20in%20%CE%B413C%20and/or%20temporal%20diachroneity%20in%20the%20initiation%20of%20cap%20carbonate%20sedimentation.%20Sedimentary%20and%20chemostratigraphic%20data%20are%20indicative%20of%20a%20Marinoan%20age%20for%20the%20Nantuo%20glaciation.%20This%20inference%20is%20supported%20by%20a%20new%20U-Pb%20zircon%20age%20of%20663%20%C2%B1%204%20Ma%20from%20a%20tuffaceous%20bed%20in%20the%20Datangpo%20Formation.%20The%20new%20date%20and%20other%20isotopic%20ages%20from%20south%20China%20constrain%20the%20age%20of%20the%20Changan%20and%20Tiesiao%20glaciation(s)%20as%20between%20761%20%C2%B1%208%20Ma%20and%20663%20%C2%B1%204%20Ma,%20and%20the%20Nantuo%20glaciation%20as%20between%20663%20%C2%B1%204%20Ma%20and%20599%20%C2%B1%204%20Ma.}}

